# shir_nodes/fs_modified_since_read.node — the `-N` file predicate.
#
# `[ -N f ]` is true iff f's modification time is strictly later than its
# access time ("modified since it was last read"). Both times come from one
# stat(2); a path that does not stat, or whose timestamp is unreadable or not
# representable as a SystemTime (pre-1970), is false — bash reports the same
# answer for a missing file and prints no diagnostic for `-N`.
#
# Out of model: `noatime`/`relatime` mounts make atime systematically stale,
# which changes the ANSWER, not the predicate — the node models the predicate.
node FsModifiedSinceRead
tag "FsModifiedSinceRead"
kind expr
field path: expr
spec: FsSemantics#modified_since_read
